course: dictionary
lesson: 3733
title: Flood: water and more
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A flood is a large amount of water covering land that is usually dry. As a verb, to flood means to cover a place with water, or to overflow. Read the words around flood to work out which meaning fits.
explain: «In a flood, move up to higher floors and never walk in floodwater, which can be fast, dirty and electrified.» The clues are move up, higher and never walk. A flood is water that is dangerous to be in.
explain: Flood has a second meaning with of. «A flood of letters» means a very large amount arriving at once. A real flood also arrives fast and in huge amounts, so the idea fits. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it.
fact: A flood is a large amount of water covering land that is usually dry.
fact: Flood can also be a verb: to flood is to cover a place with water, or to overflow.
fact: A flood of something is a very large amount arriving at once, like «a flood of letters».
fact: Floods can come from heavy rain, rivers bursting their banks, storms at sea or melting snow.
fact: Flood safety: move to higher ground, never walk, swim, cycle or drive through flood water, and listen to warnings.
exercise: «The river rose after days of rain, and the fields flooded.» What does flooded mean here? | *Covered with water | Frozen solid | Full of flowers | Dried out in the sun
exercise: In a flood, what should you do? | Swim across to check the road | *Move up to higher ground and listen to warnings | Drive through to save time | Walk through the water to get home
exercise: «A flood of letters arrived on Monday.» What does a flood of letters mean? | A few letters, sent slowly | One wet letter | *A very large amount arriving at once | A river full of paper
test: «In the flooded forest, fish eat fallen fruit and spread the seeds.» Which word here means covered by water? | fruit | seeds | *flooded | forest
test: «Fans began to flood in before the match.» What does flood in mean? | *Arrive in large numbers | Wait quietly outside | Leave early | Fall into the water
exam: Why does the Okavango river flood in the middle of the dry season? | Because fish want to swim there | Because the desert is cold at night | *Because rain that fell far away takes months to arrive | Because the river has dried up
